## Context

`slides/slides.tex` was restructured to a 5-act arc (ticket 0129)
before the three-quality argument crystallised. After 0147
(rename to argument.md) and 0149 (hypothesis extraction), the
slides need to mirror the same structure: methods + four limits,
data/answer-quality saturation through deep research,
method-quality frontier through agentic and multi-agent.

## Actions

1. Walk `slides/slides.tex`. Map each frame to a section of
   `argument.md`, or mark "out of scope" / "drop".
2. Restructure into the three-part arc:
   - Part 1 — Methods (capability ladder + four limits + scope)
   - Part 2 — Data and answer quality up to deep-research ceiling
     (regimes-scatter, ablation, hypothesis verdicts H1–H3)
   - Part 3 — Method quality and the trust frontier (verifiable /
     verified, hypothesis verdicts H4)
3. Re-render figures from updated experimental data once 0154
   produces them; until then, placeholder where data isn't ready.
4. Build with tectonic. No inline pgfplots usage — adherence test
   from ticket 0130 will fail if reintroduced. Use the Python-PDF
   pattern (ticket 0132) for new figures.
5. Slide count discipline: ≤25 frames for a typical talk.

## Exit criteria

- Slide structure mirrors argument three-part arc.
- All figures render cleanly via tectonic; no inline pgfplots.
- No frame references the old "framework" name.
- ≤25 frames in the main deck (overflow into appendix if needed).
